{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/243676-abyssal-resistance","id":243676,"title":"Abyssal Resistance?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-29T00:14:11-07:00","id":243676,"title":"Abyssal Resistance?","content":"Abyssal Resistance has Mirrors for virtually all of Solar Resistance Charms, excepting Battle Fury Focus and Bloodthirsty Sword-Dancer Spirit, both of which are berserker combat charms. Why is this? Is it simply a matter of word count, and we should just assume that Mirrors of those charms exist or can be developed? Or is this a deliberate statement about how Deathknights differ from Solars?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T08:46:43-07:00","id":244013,"title":"","content":"I don't think omission should generally be assumed to be deliberate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T09:16:53-07:00","id":244045,"title":"","content":"I think there could be room for some slight variations in the rules, though. Like possibly venting Resonance if the Abyssal goes crazy around a lot of the living and kills or severely traumatizes them, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T11:41:22-07:00","id":244224,"title":"","content":"I honestly think the Mirror idea was a product of an interesting idea turning into weak ideas. It tends to encourage not promoting unique Abyssal things and just doing Solar things, but surrounded by inky blackness. Personally, I would disallow any new uses of the Mirror keyword, and try to make new original Charms for them. <br /> <br /> The two you mention in particular, I feel, are about the passions of the Solars running amok. The Deathknights are supposed to run cold, rather than hot, so some other form of battle trance might be a better application, with different rules and effects. I have a particular hatred against the Mirror keyword right now because I was just looking over a bunch of Abyssal Charms, seeing that they were Mirrors so I had to check a different book, then check Errata in two different locations to see how they work.<br /> <br /> Still, I would throw that keyword out and bury it after rubbing it with a potato and wrapping chiken feet on strings around it to make sure it doesn't come back. New ideas are better than more Solar stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T11:55:51-07:00","id":244244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/243676-abyssal-resistance?p=244224#post244224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly think the Mirror idea was a product of an interesting idea turning into weak ideas. It tends to encourage not promoting unique Abyssal things and just doing Solar things, but surrounded by inky blackness. Personally, I would disallow any new uses of the Mirror keyword, and try to make new original Charms for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree, but the Abyssals should at least have charms that are similar, sometimes even identical to Solar charms to start with. After all, I don't think something like Salty Dog Method (from the spoilers) can really be &quot;Abyssalfied&quot; without coming of as needlessly 'eeeeeviiiiil! Boooo!!!' And later on Abyssals get access to their ghost ships with their crew of long-dead sailors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T13:01:16-07:00","id":244286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/243676-abyssal-resistance?p=244244#post244244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I completely agree, but the Abyssals should at least have charms that are similar, sometimes even identical to Solar charms to start with. After all, I don't think something like Salty Dog Method (from the spoilers) can really be &quot;Abyssalfied&quot; without coming of as needlessly 'eeeeeviiiiil! Boooo!!!' And later on Abyssals get access to their ghost ships with their crew of long-dead sailors.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, my point was they need all original ideas. Abyssals shouldn't get 'Salty Dog Method.' They should get 'Ghost Ship Rises Again.' Instead of Black Fathoms Blessed, they should get 'Ghost Ship Transcends Limits.' Instead of giving the ship crew bonuses on a port raid, they should get 'Underwater-Walking Zombie Legion.' They aren't Solars, and making them Solars just makes them lame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T13:06:41-07:00","id":244288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/243676-abyssal-resistance?p=244244#post244244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I completely agree, but the Abyssals should at least have charms that are similar, sometimes even identical to Solar charms to start with. After all, I don't think something like Salty Dog Method (from the spoilers) can really be &quot;Abyssalfied&quot; without coming of as needlessly 'eeeeeviiiiil! Boooo!!!' And later on Abyssals get access to their ghost ships with their crew of long-dead sailors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aye, they've made remarks that some Charms Abyssals get will be identical (or mostly so) to their closest comparable Solar counterparts. They're meant to serve as counterpoints to the Charms Abyssals get that diverge, sometimes sharply, from what Solars do.<br /> <br /> I've copied over a sample of revealed pre-work John did a ways back (somewhere in <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Charms#Abyssal_Charms\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>). Also, fitting you mentioned a revealed Solar Sail Charm. Perhaps Black Fathoms Blessed is a closer analogue to Ancient Mariner's Rime?<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ancient Mariner's Rime</b><br /> <b>Costs:</b> 5m; <b>Mins:</b> ???; <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Indefinite<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> ???<br /> Breathing deeply of the inimical world, the Abyssal takes in an icy tendril of death and turns undead. Her frozen corpse can withstand the subzero temperatures of unforgiving seas, and she no longer needs to breathe. While this Charm is active, death's Lawgiver may walk along the ocean's floor completely unimpeded by the ocean's pressure.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are my production notes for the Abyssal armor cascade. Charm names and effects are not final.<br /> <br /> <b>Ghost Armor Prana</b><br /> Glorious Solar Plate analog; summons a wraith of smoke and iron that forms into a suit of haunted armor. This armor can form over mundane armor, subsuming it. It can also possess mystical armor, so long as it is made of soulsteel or is deathly in nature. Armor provides defensive bonus and fanged faces in the armor can attempt to disarm weapons that strike the armor or damage unarmed attackers.<br /> <br /> <i>followed by</i><br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Torment Chains</b><br /> The deathknight\u2019s anima flares into multiple bands of pyreflame, resolving into phantom chains that orbit the Abyssal and react to her commands. Chains increase attack range and allow for several actions at range, such as grappling, lifting, pulling, and retrieving fallen weaponry.<br /> <br /> <i>followed by</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dark Headsman\u2019s Guillotine</b><br /> Death\u2019s champion summons a soulsteel guillotine to behead a victim caught in her Shadow Torment Chains.<br /> <br /> <i>followed by</i><br /> <br /> <b>Iron Maiden\u2019s Kiss</b> (apex)<br /> The deathknight wrenches her chains of torment, ripping two halves of a terrible suit of armor across the Shroud. This wicked, phantasmal armor is lined with heavy spikes, and attempts to slam shut around a victim. The grizzly armored corpses created by this Charm can be knighted by the Abyssal and welcomed into battle at her side.<br /> <br /> <i>after Ghost Armor Prana</i><br /> <br /> <b>Howling Armor Horror</b> (Upgrades Ghost Armor Prana)<br /> <br /> The Abyssal can pay to cause the armor\u2019s faces to bubble and emerge, howling and glowing with ghostflame, increasing the power of her Threaten actions. Armor whispers warnings to the deathknight, reducing the effectiveness of surprise attacks. A 2xp upgrade allows her armor\u2019s howl to unseat earthly forces and send cracks through the Shroud. When she is in or near shadowlands or places of death, her armor\u2019s howling causes earthquakes that terrify wildlife, send military units into rout, and cause movement penalties to her opponents.<br /> <br /> <i>followed by</i><br /> <br /> <b>Ravenous Blood Mist</b><br /> When the Abyssal is injured, her Ghost Armor exults, feeding on her pain and drinking her blood. With a single violent thought, the Abyssal can expel her blood in a fine mist from the faces in her haunted armor. Doing this when she is uninjured costs her lethal health levels. Her blood is full of razors, attacking on its own turn. For 2xp, death\u2019s Lawgiver may purchase an upgrade; when her attack falls on the same instant as her blood mist, she may pay 2 motes to enhance her attack with a blood razor burst. Doing so cancels her blood mist effect.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T14:29:26-07:00","id":244321,"title":"","content":"I don't mind analogs, or Charms that do similar things, but I'm pretty sure exact duplicates and the Mirror Keyword are dead as doornails. I think I saw Holden say something like that.<br /> <br /> I mean, both Abyssals and Solars getting an produce-magic-armor thing is cool, and there's a lot of room for them both to branch off into completely different direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T15:16:48-07:00","id":244363,"title":"","content":"And they will do lots of going their own ways. They will just also have a fair bit of overlap, and some of that will come in the form of some analogous Charms that are identical. I believe Holden's comment was that the Mirror setup didn't work out as well as hoped. The point to bear in mind is that <i>some</i> identical Charms is not a problem if Abyssals are well designed as a splat. Identical Charms can mean different things in the contexts of two otherwise very different Charmsets. Particularly if Abyssals have splat-specific traits beyond Charms with which to set up their context. It's a matter of not throwing them in lazily or carelessly.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EX3 What We Know Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>&quot;Q:&quot;</b> <b>Zakkeg</b><br /> From what I gather, it seems like a lot of [Abyssals'] foundational charmset will be functionally equivalent to what Solars get; it doesn't start really diverging until you go a few Charms up the tree.<br /> <br /> <b>A:</b> <b>John M\u00f8rke</b><br /> Some of their Charm trees will start off crazy different. My hope is to provide a lot of Charms that feel like mirrors without being mirrors.<br /> There will be some exact copies, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Hungry Tiger Technique. Abyssals will have an identical mechanic. Some Charms just don't get any better.<br /> 2) It is stylistically accurate to depict the Abyssals as having deep connections to the Solars. EX3 Abyssals are radically different than they have been in previous editions. Having some identical Charms to Solars is a benefit, rather than a subtraction, because it emphasizes the fact that they were / are Solars, while also making them something else.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T15:37:19-07:00","id":244373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/243676-abyssal-resistance?p=244224#post244224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Deathknights are supposed to run cold, rather than hot</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this kind of blanket statement re: how Solars/Abyssals expresso their passions ever needs to be true. It shuts out more ideas than it create if Solars always &quot;run hot&quot; and Abyssals always &quot;run cold.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T15:51:20-07:00","id":244383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/243676-abyssal-resistance?p=244373#post244373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think this kind of blanket statement re: how Solars/Abyssals expresso their passions ever needs to be true. It shuts out more ideas than it create if Solars always &quot;run hot&quot; and Abyssals always &quot;run cold.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can't tell if you are being sarcastic or not, but then I remember this was on the Exalted forums, so it doesn't matter anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T08:45:57-07:00","id":245355,"title":"","content":"I will note that the Solar berserker charms allow you to roleplay them however you want, from Berserk Rage to Stoic Determination. I will also note that I never really got why those charms were in Resistance at all. It never came up in-game, but I always thought about moving them to be the capstone charms of base Solar Hero Style. Wouldn't they fit better there (or as Solar only expansions)?<br /> <br /> As to the dev's comments, am I missing something, or are they basically saying, &quot;Yeah, Mirror charms were a wash, we're not doing that again...except when we are!&quot; I mean, Abyssal Charms being mechanically identical to Solar charms, but with darker imagery, is pretty much the very definition of Mirror Charm, isn't it?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"dat